    <!-- Content -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pb-16 lg:pb-24">
      <div class="prose prose-lg prose-blue max-w-none text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <p class="text-2xl font-medium text-gray-900 mb-8 italic">
          A penetrating sealer is the closest thing concrete has to an invisible raincoat that cannot wear off. It soaks in, reacts, and leaves the surface looking and feeling exactly as it did. That is also why it is easy to buy the wrong one: a silicate densifier and a silane water repellent look identical in the pail, yet one hardens concrete and the other keeps water out. This guide sorts the best penetrating sealers by what they actually do.
        </p>

