          </h2>

          <p>
            Densifier then repellent is the most common layering approach, and it works well on old, dusty exterior concrete. Apply the silicate first, let it react for the time stated on the label, then apply the silane-siloxane once the slab is dry. Many manufacturers publish instructions for exactly this combination.
          </p>

          <p>
