          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most exterior concrete and masonry, a water-borne silane-siloxane blend is the right penetrating sealer, and Foundation Armor SX5000 is the most versatile choice. For large salted areas, the Ghostshield 8500 concentrate gives the best cost per square foot, and Eagle Natural Seal is a sound budget option on a shorter cycle.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            When the problem is a damp basement or a dusty interior floor, a silicate is the better tool: RadonSeal Plus for below-grade concrete and Consolideck LS for interior slabs. Whatever you choose, start with clean, dry, bare concrete, apply generously within the label's window, and confirm the result with a water test.
